From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 006/NNN] system: guard the Linux-only metrics include

No field of struct sysinfo is read anywhere in this file, so the include is
only a build dependency and Darwin has no sys/sysinfo.h.

Guarding it does not make the file useful on Darwin. Every measurement here
comes from procfs: /proc/self/stat, /proc/stat, /proc/meminfo and
/proc/self/status. Each reader opens the file with an ifstream and returns a
zeroed metric when the open fails, so on Darwin the metrics report zero
rather than wrong numbers. Real values would need sysctl and
host_statistics64, which is a separate piece of work.

--- a/lib/src/system/sys_metrics_processor.cc	2026-09-03 15:13:08
+++ b/lib/src/system/sys_metrics_processor.cc	2026-09-03 15:13:54
@@ -22,7 +22,14 @@
 #include "srsran/system/sys_metrics_processor.h"
 #include <fstream>
 #include <sstream>
+/* No field of struct sysinfo is read anywhere in this file, so the include
+ * is only a build dependency. The measurements themselves come from procfs,
+ * which Darwin does not have; every reader below opens a file under /proc and
+ * returns a zeroed metric when the open fails. Process and system metrics are
+ * therefore reported as zero on Darwin rather than being wrong. */
+#ifdef __linux__
 #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
+#endif
 #include <unistd.h>
 
 using namespace srsran;
